            <ArticleTitle>[Absorption of immune complexes by neutrophils in patients with ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>56-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neutrophil absorption capacity was studied in 45 coronary patients, using immune complexes, containing various immunoglobulin classes. Neutrophil capacity for absorption increases at early stages of the disease and decreases with the progress of its duration and severity, while serum immune complex levels go up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
